{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404360-wards-101-occult-mini-subsystem","id":1404360,"title":"Wards 101 (Occult mini-subsystem)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-23T21:52:32-07:00","id":1404360,"title":"Wards 101 (Occult mini-subsystem)","content":"Do you remember wards back in second edition? Sandact remembers. They were a great defense against spirits who attempt to phase through walls and gank you in your sleep or an extra layer of security against the every annoying scrying magic. 3e claims to have wards, but they're practically a single sentence that are mentioned in sorcerous workings. How do they work mechanically? Who knows!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11ea7T_dfC8CIZzKkvYYER_RDwPAtgZn_7FHMUqGAjPs/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">So I decided to remake how Wards work in 3e</a>. It comes with a bunch of features:<ul><li>How to construct wards. Be they complex multi-generational grand seals of evil or something you just throw up for a night so House Cynis doesn't scry into your bedroom and gossip what goes on in there.</li> <li>What wards actually do and the various types of wards.</li> <li>A small smattering of Solar, Dragonblooded, and Lunar charms that interact with wards.</li> </ul><br /> Feedback is always welcomed. Hope you enjoy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T04:59:22-07:00","id":1404380,"title":"","content":"Pretty nice. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T11:12:08-07:00","id":1404434,"title":"","content":"I really like this! Very cool, much stylish! I have a charm suggestion, which I hope you will consider.<br /> I feel like there's room for the dragonblooded to also have a charm that forces a spirit to materialize. Something like an air charm, &quot;Thunderous Rebuke,&quot; with an effect like &quot;If a spirit fails to get through the ward, pay X at that moment to force it to materialize.&quot;<br /> Just an idea I had while reading through. Probably gonna put this in all my games, I love things that add a bit of magic outside the exalted specifically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T12:05:53-07:00","id":1404440,"title":"","content":"A good idea. Originally I didn't make spirits force materialize for DB's (At least at lower essences) because I thought the fire charm would be enough to see them. Forced materialization could easily be a higher essence effect tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T12:43:47-07:00","id":1404442,"title":"","content":"I'd put it right after Eye of the Far Seeing Dragon, probably? Maybe let them use that charm to activate it at a distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23941-aquatica","name":"Aquatica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23941_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T13:56:00-07:00","id":1404450,"title":"","content":"Looks cool.<br /> You currently suggest a default roll of resolve if wits+integrity isn't written. I would think resolve x2 would work better, since resolve is generally (wits+integrity)/2<br /> <br /> Unshakeable Family Foundation - I think this is a very well addition of dragonblooded family thematics.<br /> Versatile Substitution Method - protean effects generally are less abstract than this.<br /> \u200b<br /> Potentially there's room for thaumaturgy that's between mundane Occult rolls and sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T15:04:08-07:00","id":1404462,"title":"","content":"I don't hate this. Which is pretty good since the handling of wards was about 80% of why I think 2e thaumaturgy needed to fuck off and die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T15:13:44-07:00","id":1404463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404360-wards-101-occult-mini-subsystem?p=1404450#post1404450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially there's room for thaumaturgy that's between mundane Occult rolls and sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put this in thaumaturgy rules, although obviously here is a good place to come up with thaumaturgy for it.<br /> <br /> Something that gives you <b>one</b> free step on raising a specific type of ward, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, there's charmspace for &quot;the ward's maintenance need not hit the previous difficulty&quot;. It'd be extremely convenient, albeit niche. Maybe for celestial charms it could be merged into another charm's effects? Needing to hit only half the original strength to maintain it is smooth and easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T17:22:27-07:00","id":1404483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404360-wards-101-occult-mini-subsystem?p=1404450#post1404450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks cool.<br /> You currently suggest a default roll of resolve if wits+integrity isn't written. I would think resolve x2 would work better, since resolve is generally (wits+integrity)/2<br /> <br /> Unshakeable Family Foundation - I think this is a very well addition of dragonblooded family thematics.<br /> Versatile Substitution Method - protean effects generally are less abstract than this.<br /> \u200b<br /> Potentially there's room for thaumaturgy that's between mundane Occult rolls and sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea that's what I meant. The Resolve dice pool, not the Resolve score itself. It's easier to fish out what that would be as it's just Resolve 2x.<br /> <br /> I did also have some sorcery spells planned for it (Something that basically sets a long duration ward up at a significantly reduced difficulty), but I couldn't hammer it out exactly. I can always come back to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404360-wards-101-occult-mini-subsystem?p=1404463#post1404463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, there's charmspace for &quot;the ward's maintenance need not hit the previous difficulty&quot;. It'd be extremely convenient, albeit niche. Maybe for celestial charms it could be merged into another charm's effects? Needing to hit only half the original strength to maintain it is smooth and easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maintaining a ward is already half the difficulty needed to construct it. Unless you mean something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 07-24-2020, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T21:49:03-07:00","id":1404523,"title":"","content":"I meant even less, and had a brain fart there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:49:58-07:00","id":1404539,"title":"","content":"I found half pretty generous. I meant a ward that lasts a decade and covers an entire district of Nexus only has a difficulty to maintain of 5. With charms this is doable, hell even a mortal is within the realm of feasibility to pull it off (Yes I know Intelligence 5 Occult 5 mortals don't grow on trees, but still pretty low difficulty given what wards can do). Hell, I was even fairly generous with modifiers on constructing or maintaining wards.<br /> <br /> Wards that cover huge areas and last for a decade are very difficult by design. Actually making them then having enough strength to actually ward things off vs how long/how big you want a ward is something I thought would be an interesting payoff. I thought about increasing the math a bit more, but I wanna test them out and see how they work in games before fiddling with the math on some charms anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}